@title STORY • DIGGY: DOUBLE SHIFTS
@bg diggy_kitchen_morning
You're Duncan Williams. It's 5:10 a.m. Kiara's asleep on the couch in her school clothes because she wanted to be "ready early." Your mama's already at her first job.
Diggy: (whispering) Kiara. Kiara. Bed. Real bed.
Kiara: (half asleep) Is the mean lady coming to my recital again?
Diggy: She's not mean.
Kiara: You said she was mean.
Diggy: I said it nice.
You leave a note on the fridge, take the 5:40 bus to campus, and get to the track before the sun. Before London. Every day. She doesn't know that part.
@bg track_stadium_morning
@show coachm
Coach M: Williams! Why are you always here before me? It's disrespectful.
> [Good] "Bus schedule, Coach." -> a1
> [Bold] "'Cause I want your 200 record." -> a2
> [Sweet] "Honestly? It's the only quiet part of my day." -> a3
*a1
Coach M: Respect. Bus life builds legs.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Diggy_Fire 2
Coach M: (grinning) Oh, you WANT it want it? Strides. Now. Let's see.
@jump a_done
*a3
@add Coach_Bond 2
Coach M stops joking. He sits on the bleacher next to you for a minute, the two of you watching the sun come up over the field.
Coach M: I used to come early too. My pops worked nights. Track was the only place nobody needed nothing from me.
*a_done
@bg restaurant_night
@show cassie
Friday night at Casa Morales. Twelve tables. A birthday party of twenty. Cassie seating people like air traffic control.
Cassie: Table nine. The Sterlings' friends. Rich people tip bad, by the way. Watch.
Ms. Morales: (from the kitchen) DUNCAN. Your plates are dying.
You carry four plates up each arm. You've done this since sixteen.
> [Bold] Charm the whole birthday party. Sing with them. -> b1
> [Good] Head down. Fast. Perfect. -> b2
> [Sweet] Help Cassie when the host stand gets slammed. -> b3
*b1
@add Tips 3
You lead "Las Mañanitas" at full volume. Ms. Morales comes out of the kitchen to watch. The table leaves you a hundred dollars and a phone number you throw away on the way to the back.
@jump b_done
*b2
@add Tips 2
@add Ms_Morales 2
Ms. Morales: (passing you) That's why you're my favorite. Don't tell Cassie.
@jump b_done
*b3
@add Cassie_Friendship 3
Cassie: (when it's over) You didn't have to do that.
Diggy: You'd have done it for me.
Cassie: ...I'd have charged you a smoothie.
*b_done
@bg bus_stop_night
Midnight bus home. Your feet hurt. You count your tips under a streetlight. You put most of it in the envelope for the light bill.
Your phone buzzes. London: "did u eat tonight"
She asks that a lot lately. Like it matters to her.
> [Sweet] "yeah. did you?" -> c1
> [Bold] "why u worried about me sterling" -> c2
> [Good] Send her a picture of the staff meal. -> c3
*c1
London: "yes. pancakes. dont make it weird"
You don't make it weird. You smile at your phone the whole ride home.
@jump end
*c2
London: "im not. go to sleep williams"
Five minutes later: "but did you"
@jump end
*c3
London: "that looks better than my chef's food"
London: "dont tell him i said that"
*end
Diggy Williams carries a lot. He's never once let anybody see him put it down.
